Simpleton: MPD aborted at every stop - the SACD/DSDIFF plugins' finish().

Both plugins' finish() call container_update(nullptr) to let go of the open
container.  container_update() begins with AllocatedPath(path_fs), whose
constructor copies path_fs.c_str() into a std::string; a null pointer there
throws std::logic_error ("basic_string: construction from null is not
valid").  finish() is noexcept, so the exception became std::terminate and
MPD died with SIGABRT on every shutdown - systemd's "status=6/ABRT" on each
stop and restart since the plugins went in (seen 27 Sep, 1 Oct, 11 Oct 2026;
the 27 Sep "hot-swap crash" was this, during a restart by simpleton-dac-detect).

A null path now releases the reader and the media and returns false, which
is what finish() wanted.  No other caller passes a null path.

--- a/src/decoder/plugins/SacdIsoDecoderPlugin.cxx
+++ b/src/decoder/plugins/SacdIsoDecoderPlugin.cxx
@@ -80,6 +80,23 @@
 
 static bool
 container_update(Path path_fs) {
+	/* Simpleton: finish() calls this with nullptr to let the container go.
+	   AllocatedPath(Path) copies path_fs.c_str() into a std::string, and a
+	   null pointer there throws std::logic_error - inside a noexcept
+	   function, so MPD aborted (status=6/ABRT) at every stop. Release
+	   the container here instead. */
+	if (path_fs.IsNull()) {
+		if (sacd_reader) {
+			sacd_reader->close();
+			sacd_reader.reset();
+		}
+		if (sacd_media) {
+			sacd_media->close();
+			sacd_media.reset();
+		}
+		sacd_path.SetNull();
+		return false;
+	}
 	auto curr_path = AllocatedPath(path_fs);
 	if (!FileExists(curr_path)) {
 		curr_path = path_fs.GetDirectoryName();
